WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.347
Hi, I'm Tango!

00:00:02.347 --> 00:00:07.282
Here's how vLLM tunes serving for a two point four trillion parameter hybrid model.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.205
The key: on a hybrid model, the linear layers' fixed state sets

00:00:14.205 --> 00:00:16.307
the page size for the attention layers.

00:00:20.258 --> 00:00:22.255
A request brings an eight-thousand-token prompt.

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:25.917
Prefill engines read it all at once and build its cache.

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:30.005
The cache moves to separate decode engines, and the hand-off only works

00:00:30.005 --> 00:00:32.451
if both sides use the same block size.

00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:35.436
Decode writes the answer, one token per step.

00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:41.992
Sixty-nine gated DeltaNet layers, twenty-three full-attention layers, and one block size

00:00:41.992 --> 00:00:43.632
that must hold either.

00:00:44.052 --> 00:00:47.749
DeltaNet keeps one fixed state per request, however long the prompt.

00:00:48.169 --> 00:00:50.075
Full attention grows token by token.

00:00:51.605 --> 00:00:54.968
One state equals two thousand one hundred and eight tokens.

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:59.003
Rounded to sixteen, every block is two thousand one hundred and twelve.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.969
Then walk down the memory ladder the server prints at startup.

00:01:03.969 --> 00:01:07.971
Sharded one way, an engine's cache holds a hundred and twelve requests.

00:01:07.971 --> 00:01:09.972
Sharded wider, a hundred and eighty.

00:01:11.442 --> 00:01:14.504
Check the CUDA graph estimate, because it's charged to your cache.

00:01:14.924 --> 00:01:19.515
Benchmark prefill and decode as separate workloads, then combine only the winners.

00:01:19.935 --> 00:01:22.030
Find where speculation stops paying.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:27.058
Two doublings past concurrency two fifty-six, it costs sixty-two percent of throughput.

00:01:28.767 --> 00:01:32.185
On a hybrid model, price the linear layers first: they set the

00:01:32.185 --> 00:01:34.749
block size and a fixed share of every request.

00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:40.788
To recap: price the cache, let the linear layers set the block,

00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:42.165
and tune each phase alone.

00:01:42.585 --> 00:01:44.589
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:44.589 --> 00:01:45.162
I'm Tango.

00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:45.448
Bye!
